    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Example 2",
     "statement": "Find the line through $(3,-2)$ perpendicular to $2x+3y=6$.",
     "steps": [
      "$3y=-2x+6$ so the gradient is $-\\frac{2}{3}$; the perpendicular gradient is $\\frac{3}{2}$.",
      "$y+2=\\frac{3}{2}(x-3)$, so $2y+4=3x-9$.",
      "Rearrange: $3x-2y-13=0$. Check $(3,-2)$: $9+4-13=0$."
     ],
     "answer": "$3x-2y-13=0$"
    }
